{
  "text": " Importantly, there are now two analyses I think everyone should be aware of. One is by Tracy Hogue from the U.S.A. California, Davis. It was published in late August where she used the VERS in v-safe data. And she analyzed reports of myocarditis. This is heart inflammation. I told you I'm a cardiologist. I've seen this. I know exactly what I'm talking about here. The vaccine has the ability to seed cells in the heart with lipid nanoparticles. We believe the cell line is called pericytes. They are around blood vessels and they support cardiomyocytes, the main contractile cells in the heart. And it's now known that the vaccine itself from preclinical and clinical observations causes myocarditis. It's not a conjecture. The vaccines cause myocarditis, particularly Pfizer and Moderna. And I anticipate with enough data, enough exposure, it'll also be with J&J, AstraZeneca and the other vaccines available.",
